From 2f0ececa7b5e5f7b7db42cabef53093361b4e84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Bates <help@batesai.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:08:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Subject Mastery contract v2: profile + plan documents,
 nested lesson keys

The shared contract gained "v2 additions" while this branch was being
built. This brings the API up to it:

- Progress keys accept the v2 regex (subject plus 2-7 more ids, so
  lessons can sit in nested topics).
- GET/PUT /api/subjectmastery/profile and /plan: whole documents, last
  write wins on updatedAt, stored in new sm_profile / sm_plan tables
  (migrations/0002_sm_profile_plan.sql). Shape and size are checked the
  way the player's normalizers produce them; an avatar must be a
  png/jpeg/webp data: URL; unknown fields are dropped.
- The progress merge now matches the player's mergeRecord() exactly: a
  newer in_progress keeps a stored completed/known status but takes the
  newer position and time, and equal timestamps break by status rank,
  then position. Duplicate keys in one PUT are applied in order by SQLite
  instead of being pre-folded in JavaScript, which the convergence test
  showed is not equivalent.
- Account deletion also clears sm_profile and sm_plan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
